<Base lang="en" route="responsible" title="Responsible Gambling · Veintiuno" description="Warning signs that gambling is becoming a problem, and where to find free, confidential help in the US, UK and elsewhere.">
  <div class="container legal">
    <div class="read prose">
      <h1>Responsible gambling</h1>
      <p class="lead">Veintiuno is an educational tool: there’s no real-money play in the app. But if you play in casinos, keep this in mind.</p>
      <h2>Simple rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Decide how much money and time you’ll spend before you start, and stick to it.</li>
        <li>Only play with money you can afford to lose. Never with borrowed money.</li>
        <li>Don’t chase losses by raising your bets.</li>
        <li>Blackjack has a house edge: over time, you lose. Treat it as the cost of entertainment.</li>
        <li>Don’t gamble to escape problems, or after drinking.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Warning signs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You think about gambling constantly or need bigger bets to feel the same.</li>
        <li>You lie about how much you play or lose.</li>
        <li>You’ve tried to cut back or stop and couldn’t.</li>
        <li>Gambling is causing money, work or family problems.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Where to get help</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>United States:</strong> call or text <strong>1-800-GAMBLER</strong> (National Council on Problem Gambling), free and confidential, 24/7.</li>
        <li><strong>United Kingdom:</strong> National Gambling Helpline <strong>0808 8020 133</strong> (GamCare), or <a href="https://www.begambleaware.org" rel="noopener">BeGambleAware.org</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Spain:</strong> <a href="https://www.jugarbien.es" rel="noopener">jugarbien.es</a> and FEJAR, <strong>900 200 225</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Elsewhere:</strong> look for your country’s public problem-gambling service, or talk to your doctor.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Asking for help isn’t failure. Gambling disorder is a recognized condition, and it’s treatable.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
